            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed both added files in full. CheckRisk is fail-closed: it returns nil only for the exact string 'none'; every other input (empty, case variants, whitespace, multi-digit, duplicates, non-ASCII digits) returns ErrInvalidRisk or ErrHighRisk. riskItem requires a single byte in '1'..'6', so a non-ASCII digit cannot pass, and the seen slice is indexed only after riskItem validates 1..6, so there is no out-of-range access.",
              "CheckReport delegates to reviewverdict.ParseReport and Clear, and propagates any parse error. It cannot return nil on a parse failure.",
              "The candidate adds no I/O, no secrets, no dependencies, no network or filesystem access, and no authorization surface. Neither file stores or executes anything. Its stated enforcement point lives in a separate command and delivery check that is not part of this candidate. No reachable exploit or data-exposure path is evidenced, so there are no risk findings."
            ]
          }
