            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "CheckRisk returns nil only for the exact string \"none\". An empty string, whitespace, a different case, multi-byte digits, two-digit numbers, repeated items, empty list entries and \"none\" inside a list all fail the single-byte digit check or the duplicate check, so each returns ErrInvalidRisk. This fails closed, and the cases are deterministic and independent of input order.",
              "Valid item lists always return an error wrapping ErrHighRisk and name each item in the order written. Both error classes are asserted with errors.Is in both directions, so the two cases cannot be confused.",
              "The upper bound byte('0'+len(highRiskItems)) is a constant expression over an array length, so it compiles and accepts exactly the digits 1 to 6. The tests cover the boundary values 0, 7 and 10.",
              "CheckReport delegates entirely to reviewverdict.ParseReport and Clear and returns their errors unchanged. The tests assert the wrapped sentinel for each failure class: unparseable, unknown member, outside enum, missing evidence and not clear. I could not see reviewverdict in this candidate, so those sentinels are assumed to exist.",
              "The tests use no shared mutable state, no time dependence and no parallel subtests, so the map-iteration closures and the order of cases do not make them flaky."
            ]
          }
